// Test: a nested element type is reserved, not silently read as two literals.
//
// `[][]i64` has no meaning yet -- the `[]T` type parsers do not recurse, so the type cannot
// be written on the other side of a signature. What it must not do is parse as `[]` followed
// by `[]i64`, which left a value on the stack and reported the function's stack effect
// instead of the real problem.
fn main() {
	[][]i64 -> g
	g len print nl
}
